From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: axp20x: declare the AXP2101 power-key cell

The pending AXP2101 series defines AXP2101_IRQ_PEK_RIS_EDGE and
AXP2101_IRQ_PEK_FAL_EDGE in the header, but never adds the axp20x-pek cell to
axp2101_cells[]. The interrupt numbers exist; the device does not.

The effect is silent: axp20x-pek can never probe because the MFD never creates
it, so the top-left button is simply not visible to Linux, with no error
anywhere. Every other axp20x variant that has a power key lists the cell --
AXP717 next to this one does:

    axp717_cells[]   regulator, axp20x-pek, axp717-adc, usb-power, battery
    axp2101_cells[]  regulator,                      usb-power, battery

Add the cell with the two edge interrupts, matching the AXP717 shape. The
driver uses PEK_DBR (rising, pressed) and PEK_DBF (falling, released).

This depends on the PMU interrupt being usable, which needs GPIO7 pulled up in
the DTS -- a LEVEL_LOW IRQ on a floating pin storms and hangs the boot. With
the pull-up in place both this and the RTC's interrupt resolve:

    /proc/interrupts
     7:  esp32xx-gpio  1  pcf85063
     8:  esp32xx-gpio  7  axp2101_irq_chip

--- a/drivers/mfd/axp20x.c	2026-11-08 13:36:44.783117384 -0700
+++ drivers/mfd/axp20x.c	2026-11-08 13:36:44.794938037 -0700
@@ -1142,9 +1142,21 @@
 	DEFINE_RES_IRQ_NAMED(AXP2101_IRQ_VBUS_REMOVAL, "VBUS_REMOVAL"),
 };
 
+/*
+ * Escapement: the power key. The series defines AXP2101_IRQ_PEK_RIS_EDGE and
+ * _FAL_EDGE in the header but never declares the pek cell below, so
+ * axp20x-pek could never probe -- the MFD simply never created the device.
+ * Every other axp20x variant that has a power key lists it.
+ */
+static const struct resource axp2101_pek_resources[] = {
+	DEFINE_RES_IRQ_NAMED(AXP2101_IRQ_PEK_RIS_EDGE, "PEK_DBR"),
+	DEFINE_RES_IRQ_NAMED(AXP2101_IRQ_PEK_FAL_EDGE, "PEK_DBF"),
+};
+
 /* No driver handles its fuel gauge yet. */
 static struct mfd_cell axp2101_cells[] = {
 	MFD_CELL_NAME("axp20x-regulator"),
+	MFD_CELL_RES("axp20x-pek", axp2101_pek_resources),
 	MFD_CELL_OF("axp20x-usb-power-supply",
 		    axp2101_usb_power_supply_resources, NULL, 0, 0,
 		    "x-powers,axp2101-usb-power-supply"),
